+// must treat exactly. A ring entry is only a cache of "the resume pc of the call made
+// with this sp, and where its continuation is"; every case below makes a RET whose
+// target is not that (or whose entry was overwritten, or never written), so the pop
+// must fall back to the dispatch template, and the ones that do match must still be
+// exact. Run in every mode (KJIT_RETCONT=0, 1, 2); the cold/warm differential check
+// compares each case with the original code.
+//
+//   make harness-test-asm ASM=tests/arm64/ring_returns.s HOT_SVC_SYMBOL=ring_longjmp_mark
+//
+// Initial fixture state: x12 = FIXTURE_DATA_BASE, a 16 KiB RW window (all zero); SP and
+// x30 are 0, so every case builds its stack inside the window. Every case ends in a
+// `ret` to the entry x30 (0): an unreadable target, where the run returns to userspace
+// (and where an empty ring entry, pc 0 and host 0, must not match).
